%erg 0.1
Title: Zotero: local-first library index for report runs
Created: 2026-10-15
Author: Claude

--- log ---
2026-10-15T17:55Z Claude created

--- body ---
## Context
`scripts/zotero.py` (backend of the `zotero` skill) reads the library through
two surfaces only: the desktop `zotero.sqlite` for `probe`, `match` and
`dedup-report`, and the Web API index (`load_index` → `build_index`, 24 h
cache) for `audit`, `reconcile`, `sync-index` and `match --source api`. It
never calls the client's local HTTP API (`127.0.0.1:23119/api/`).

Consequence: `audit` and `reconcile` pay a full Web API rebuild even on a
machine whose `zotero.sqlite` is present. Ticket 1113 records that cost
(rebuild killed at 300 s on doudou). Ticket 0455 already proposed "local
server when the client answers, Web API otherwise", deferred to the tooling
review of 0485; `docs/zotero-integration.md` §5 justifies sqlite + Web API by
headless runs, which holds for nightbeat/beat but not for interactive runs.

## Scope
Report-mode reads only. The `--apply` fresh recheck under the injection lock
stays on the Web API: writes go to the server, so dedup must see server state
(a local mirror can lag a sync). Its cost belongs to 1113 (`since=` delta).
Local-API or connector writes are out of scope (0485 tooling review first).

## Options to decide before code
1. Build the index from `zotero.sqlite` (`items`, `itemAttachments.storageHash`
   = md5, titles/DOIs), opened `?immutable=1`. No client, no network.
2. Local HTTP API, when the client answers and `extensions.zotero.httpServer`
   allows it. Same JSON shape as the Web API, so `build_index` could take a
   base URL. Needs the client running.
3. `pyzotero` with `local=True` for (2) instead of stdlib HTTP, per §5 of the
   integration doc. Adds a dependency (`uv`); weigh against reusing the
   existing stdlib paging.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] Measure: an index from local sqlite on doudou is equivalent to the Web
      API index for the fields `audit`/`reconcile` use (md5, keys, parents,
      titles, DOIs), and its build time is recorded
- [ ] `audit` and report-mode `reconcile` use the local source when present
      and fresh enough, record `"source"` in the report, and fall back to the
      Web API otherwise
- [ ] `reconcile --apply` behaviour unchanged (fresh Web API recheck under lock)
- [ ] `docs/zotero-integration.md` §5 updated to state the read order
- [ ] `make check` passes
